# SEO metadata and share previews

## Never truncate with an ellipsis

- No title, meta description, `og:title`, `og:description`, `twitter:title`, `twitter:description`, `seoTitle`, or `seoDescription` may end with `...` or `…`. Search engines and share cards show these as broken snippets.
- Write copy that fits instead of cutting it: titles **≤ 60 chars** (before the `| T-Compare` suffix), descriptions **120-160 chars**, ending in a complete sentence.
- When text is generated from data, pass it through `metaDescription()` / `metaTitle()` in `app/lib/seo.ts`. They drop whole trailing sentences or cut at a word boundary and close with a period. Never hand-roll `slice(...) + "..."` for metadata.

## Every indexable page must have

- Unique `title` and `description`.
- `alternates: canonicalAlternates(path)` (absolute `https://www.t-compare.com` URL).
- `openGraph: { ...OG_BASE, title, description, url }` (page `openGraph` replaces the parent's, so always spread `OG_BASE`) and `twitter: { card: "summary_large_image", title, description }`.
- A preview image: an `opengraph-image.tsx` in the route segment using `renderOgCard` from `app/lib/og-card.tsx` (1200×630 with `alt`), or inherit one from a parent segment. Do not set `openGraph.images` by hand unless the file is in `public/og/`.
- One `<h1>` and relevant JSON-LD (at least `BreadcrumbList` via `breadcrumbListSchema`).
- New public routes must appear in `app/sitemap.ts`. Non-indexable utility pages get `robots: { index: false, follow: true }`.

## Enforcement

`npm run build` runs `npm run check:seo-meta` (`scripts/audit-seo-meta.mjs`) after the build. It reads every prerendered page and **fails the build** on an ellipsis ending or a missing title, description, canonical, OG, or Twitter tag, or a missing preview image. Fix the page; do not weaken the check.
